  "headline": "Galle Fort: Dutch Ramparts, Spice Mansions & Bastion Sunsets",
  "description": "Built by the Portuguese and fortified by the Dutch East India Company, Galle Fort is still a living town: families fly kites from the coral-stone bastions, church bells ring over quiet lanes and merchant mansions have become small galleries and courtyard cafés.\n\nI walk the ramparts with you at golden hour, open doors to hidden Dutch courtyards and stay in restored villas inside the walls so that the fort is yours again once the day visitors leave.",
